#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# log10

#% text
# `log10(x)` gives the base-10 logarithm of `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# An exact power of 10 gives its exponent; any other argument becomes `log(x)/log(10)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
log10(10^5)
#% output
#= 5

#% cell
log10(1/10)
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
log10(x)
#% output
#= log(x)/log(10)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
log10(3.0)
#% output
#= 0.47712125471966244

#% cell
n(log10(3), 25)
#% output
#= 0.4771212547196624372950279033

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `log_base`, `exp`
